      "sequence_position": 6,
      "problem": "Given a cylinder, find the differential $\\text{d}V$ for the volume $V$ of the cylinder if the radius is $r=2$ and the height is $h=4.$",
      "worked_solution": "The volume of the cylinder is $V=\\pi {r}^{2}h.$ Let's find the differential:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(r,h) & =(\\frac{∂V}{∂r})\\,\\text{d}r+(\\frac{∂V}{∂h})\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =2\\pi rh\\,\\text{d}r+\\pi {r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor $r=2$ and $h=4,$ the differential is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{d}V(2,4) & =2\\pi \\cdot 2\\cdot 4\\,\\text{d}r+\\pi \\cdot {2}^{2}\\,\\text{d}h \\\\  & =16\\pi \\,\\text{d}r+4\\pi \\,\\text{d}h.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
